      en: "The Yagodina Karst area is located in the western Rhodopes of southern Bulgaria, known for spectacular karst formations, caves, and deep gorges. The terrain is composed of limestone, shaped by millennia of erosion. Yagodina Cave, one of the longest in Bulgaria, extends for several kilometers and hosts underground lakes and stalactites. The karst landscape provides habitat for rare bat species and endemic cave insects. The region is also known for its traditional villages and cultivation of tobacco and potatoes. The area offers numerous hiking trails and is a popular destination for speleologists.",
